# Day 4 — Field Notes. 25 August. Breezy. Errand: Augie's month-end round —
# the rain gauge in the meadow, the spring, a stone for the cairn. Dot starts asking
# what the mountain sounds like, and the sound log becomes something they share.

call D4_AM
  day 4
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Morning. Readings? Over.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
  > "Not yet. Coffee first." -> coffee
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry bulb {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}.
DOT  Copy all. You're getting fast at that.
goto plan
node coffee
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Not yet. Coffee first.
DOT  Hit it on the left. I'll write "breezy."
node plan
DOT  End of the month, Kestrel. Augie did a round. Rain gauge down in the meadow, the spring, and a stone on the cairn up on the ridge.
DOT  Don't ask me about the stone. I asked him once and he talked for forty minutes.
choice
  > "What's the rain gauge for? It hasn't rained." -> gauge
  > "I'll do the round." -> round
node gauge
THEO What's the rain gauge for? It hasn't rained in weeks.
DOT  It's for writing down zero. Somebody has to. Over.
node round
do errand Augie's round: the rain gauge in the meadow, the spring, and a stone for the cairn.
DOT  Basin out.

call D4_GAUGE
  day 4
  needs gauge_read
  after D4_AM
  kind small
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. What's the gauge say?
THEO Zero.
DOT  Zero. Again. Write it down anyway.
THEO Why?
DOT  Because one day it won't be, and you'll want to know how long it was. Basin out.

call D4_SOUND
  day 4-11
  needs sound_logged
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Can I ask you a strange one?
THEO Go ahead.
DOT  What does it sound like up there? No, really. Describe it. I've been on this desk nineteen years and I've only ever heard it through your microphone.
choice
  > "Like a room after the party." -> party
  > "Like a piano with the lid down." -> lid
  > "It sounds like nothing. Then it doesn't." -> nothing
node party
THEO Like a room after the party's gone home. Things still settling.
DOT  Huh.
goto more
node lid
THEO Like a piano with the lid down. You can tell there's something in there.
DOT  Huh.
goto more
node nothing
THEO It sounds like nothing. Then you wait, and it doesn't.
DOT  Huh.
node more
DOT  Keep doing that. Write them down. When you call in, tell me one. Augie never did. He said I wouldn't get it.
DOT  Basin out.

call D4_CAIRN
  day 4
  needs cairn_stone
  after D4_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You up on the ridge?
THEO I put a stone on the cairn. It felt silly.
DOT  He said every stone was a season. Count them.
choice
  > Count them. -> count
  > "I'd rather not know." -> rather
node count
THEO ...Twenty-two. Twenty-three, now.
DOT  ...Twenty-three. Okay. That's the round. Thank you, Kestrel.
goto out
node rather
THEO I'd rather not know.
DOT  There are twenty-two. Twenty-three, now. Sorry. I counted for you.
node out
do errand_done
DOT  Basin out.

call D4_EVE
  day 4
  time 16:30-18:00
  retry 20:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Evening readings, and one sound.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_pm set gave_readings -> read
  > "No readings. Just a sound." -> sound
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}.
DOT  Copy. And the sound?
node sound
THEO The wind in the tower. It's not one note. It's two, a hair apart.
DOT  The wobble.
THEO The wobble.
DOT  Goodnight, Kestrel.
